---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const lastUpdated = "September 9, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Maryam Akhyani"
  description="How this website and Maryam Akhyani's personal Google API automation handle data."
  currentPath="/privacy"
>
  <!-- Logo -->
  <a href="/" class="logo" title="Maryam Akhyani"></a>

  <section class="legal-section">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <h2>Who this covers</h2>
      <p>
        This policy covers two things: the website at www.maryamakhyani.com, and a
        personal automation tool registered with Google as an OAuth application
        under the name "local gws". Both are operated by Maryam Akhyani as an
        individual. There is no company, no team, and no commercial service behind
        either one.
      </p>

      <h2>The website</h2>
      <p>
        This site is a static portfolio. It does not ask you to create an account,
        it does not run advertising, and it does not sell or share information about
        visitors. Standard server request logs may be recorded by the hosting
        provider, Vercel, as part of delivering the site. If you choose to contact
        me through a form or by email, your message and email address are used only
        to reply to you.
      </p>

      <h2>The personal Google automation</h2>
      <p>
        The OAuth application "local gws" is a private tool with exactly one user:
        Maryam Akhyani. It is not offered to the public and no one else can sign in
        to it. It exists to read her own Gmail mailbox so that incoming newsletters
        can be summarised into a personal daily reading digest.
      </p>
      <p>Specifically:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          It requests read access to her own Gmail messages, and permission to send
          the resulting digest email to her own address.
        </li>
        <li>
          It runs locally on her own computer. Message content is processed there and
          the resulting notes are stored in her private notes folder on that same
          machine.
        </li>
        <li>
          It never accesses any other person's mailbox, because no other person can
          authorise it.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How Google user data is used</h2>
      <p>
        Use of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
        <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
        including the Limited Use requirements.
      </p>
      <p>In plain terms, data obtained from Google APIs is:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Used only to produce Maryam Akhyani's own personal reading digest.</li>
        <li>Never sold, rented, or shared with third parties.</li>
        <li>Never used for advertising, profiling, or any commercial purpose.</li>
        <li>Never used to train generalised machine learning models.</li>
        <li>
          Not transferred to any human other than the account owner herself, and not
          transferred to any server operated by anyone else.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
      <p>
        Mail content fetched by the automation is held only for as long as it takes to
        produce that day's digest. The digest notes it produces live in a private local
        folder and can be deleted at any time. Access can be revoked at any time from the
        Google Account permissions page, which immediately stops all further access.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy can be sent to Maryam Akhyani through the contact
        details on the <a href="/">home page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .legal-section {
    padding: 8rem 0 6rem;
  }

  .legal-section .container {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  .legal-section h1 {
    font-family: "Playfair Display", serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .updated {
    color: #777;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }

  .legal-section h2 {
    font-family: "Playfair Display", serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: 2.5rem 0 0.75rem;
    color: #d96d2b;
  }

  .legal-section p,
  .legal-section li {
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: #333;
  }

  .legal-section ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
    margin: 0.75rem 0;
  }

  .legal-section li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .legal-section a {
    color: #d96d2b;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .legal-section {
      padding: 6rem 0 4rem;
    }
  }
</style>
